<li><a href="https://earthstar-project.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Earthstar</a>, a decentralized database with no traditional accounts that syncs by ranges, today on top of Willow.</li>
<li><a href="http://ftsc.org/docs/fts-0004.001" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">FTS-0004 EchoMail Specification</a> from the FTSC, where FidoNet's <code>MSGID</code> and <code>SEEN-BY</code> live.</li>
<li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FidoNet" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">FidoNet</a> on Wikipedia, for the history of Tom Jennings' BBS network and its nightly sync model.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/activitypub/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">ActivityPub</a>, the W3C recommendation. The inbox-delivery model that dispatches instead of reconciling.</li>
<li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Merkle_tree" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Merkle tree</a> and Apache Cassandra's <a href="https://cassandra.apache.org/doc/latest/cassandra/managing/operating/repair.html" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">anti-entropy</a>, for the step before range-based reconciliation.</li>
<li><a href="https://bsky.social/about/blog/4-13-2023-moderation" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Composable Moderation</a> on the Bluesky blog, the model of labelers you subscribe to.</li>
<li><a href="https://nlp.stanford.edu/pubs/eigentrust.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">The EigenTrust Algorithm for Reputation Management in P2P Networks</a>, the transitive reputation that isolates the Sybil attack.</li>
<li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NoCeM" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">NoCeM</a>, the signed spam notices on Usenet in the nineties, ancestor of composable labels.</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/2color/awesome-prolly-tree" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Prolly Trees</a> and Merkle Search Trees, variants of the Merkle tree whose shape is derived from the content and not from the insertion order.</li>
<li><a href="https://blog.joinmastodon.org/2025/10/mastodon-4-5-for-devs/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Mastodon 4.5 for Developers</a>, which enables fetching a thread's missing replies by default.</li>
